IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `saa-formulas`

-- Student Assistance Act 1973, ss 9C, 9CA(2), 9D, 10F, 10G, 12ZK, 12ZLB, 12ZLC, 43E(5), (6) -- worked cases for saa-formulas.l4.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were worked by hand from the
-- text and the sidecar formulas before running. The student, Jarrah, and every figure are the encoder's (hypothetical), as in
-- saa-cases-student.l4; the minimum repayment income of $67,000 is ILLUSTRATIVE (it is indexed under HESA s 154-25).

§ `ss 9C, 9CA(2), 9D -- the accumulated debt`

-- A former accumulated debt of $1,851.20 (saa-cases-student.l4's 2024-25 example, used here for a later year) plus a $1,025 loan
-- incurred July to December, nothing repaid: $2,876.20, cents disregarded, $2,876.
#ASSERT `What is my accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt` 1851.20 1025 0 FALSE EQUALS 2876
-- For 2024-25 (s 9CA(2)): $1,000 + ($1,025 - $25) x 0.8 = $1,800.
#ASSERT `What is my accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt` 1000 1025 25 TRUE EQUALS 1800
-- Under $1 is taken to be zero (s 9D(2)).
#ASSERT `What is my accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt` 0 0.5 0 FALSE EQUALS 0

§ `HESA s 154-20(2), as s 10F(1) adopts it`

-- $80,000 against a $67,000 minimum: 15% of $13,000 = $1,950.
#ASSERT `What is the s 154-20(2) amount` 80000 67000 125000 EQUALS 1950
-- $150,000: 15% of $58,000 = $8,700, plus 17% of $25,000 = $4,250: $12,950.
#ASSERT `What is the s 154-20(2) amount` 150000 67000 125000 EQUALS 12950

§ `ss 10F, 12ZK, 12ZLC -- the compulsory repayment`

`Jarrah on 80000 with a 3000 debt` MEANS `My compulsory repayment facts` WITH
    `my repayment income` IS 80000
    `the minimum repayment income` IS 67000
    `the s 154-20(2) upper threshold` IS 125000
    `I had an accumulated debt on the 1 June` IS TRUE
    `my accumulated debt on that 1 June` IS 3000
    `amounts paid or assessed against that debt` IS 0
    `my Medicare levy is nil or reduced` IS FALSE
    `my other income-contingent loan repayments for the year` IS 0
    `the income year is 2019-20 or later` IS TRUE

`Jarrah with HELP repayments of 1950` MEANS `My compulsory repayment facts` WITH
    `my repayment income` IS 80000
    `the minimum repayment income` IS 67000
    `the s 154-20(2) upper threshold` IS 125000
    `I had an accumulated debt on the 1 June` IS TRUE
    `my accumulated debt on that 1 June` IS 3000
    `amounts paid or assessed against that debt` IS 0
    `my Medicare levy is nil or reduced` IS FALSE
    `my other income-contingent loan repayments for the year` IS 1950
    `the income year is 2019-20 or later` IS TRUE

`Jarrah with 1000 left and HELP repayments of 500` MEANS `My compulsory repayment facts` WITH
    `my repayment income` IS 80000
    `the minimum repayment income` IS 67000
    `the s 154-20(2) upper threshold` IS 125000
    `I had an accumulated debt on the 1 June` IS TRUE
    `my accumulated debt on that 1 June` IS 3000
    `amounts paid or assessed against that debt` IS 2000
    `my Medicare levy is nil or reduced` IS FALSE
    `my other income-contingent loan repayments for the year` IS 500
    `the income year is 2019-20 or later` IS TRUE

`Jarrah at the minimum` MEANS `My compulsory repayment facts` WITH
    `my repayment income` IS 67000
    `the minimum repayment income` IS 67000
    `the s 154-20(2) upper threshold` IS 125000
    `I had an accumulated debt on the 1 June` IS TRUE
    `my accumulated debt on that 1 June` IS 3000
    `amounts paid or assessed against that debt` IS 0
    `my Medicare levy is nil or reduced` IS FALSE
    `my other income-contingent loan repayments for the year` IS 0
    `the income year is 2019-20 or later` IS TRUE

`Jarrah with a reduced Medicare levy` MEANS `My compulsory repayment facts` WITH
    `my repayment income` IS 80000
    `the minimum repayment income` IS 67000
    `the s 154-20(2) upper threshold` IS 125000
    `I had an accumulated debt on the 1 June` IS TRUE
    `my accumulated debt on that 1 June` IS 3000
    `amounts paid or assessed against that debt` IS 0
    `my Medicare levy is nil or reduced` IS TRUE
    `my other income-contingent loan repayments for the year` IS 0
    `the income year is 2019-20 or later` IS TRUE

`an FS debtor in 2018-19` MEANS `My compulsory repayment facts` WITH
    `my repayment income` IS 80000
    `the minimum repayment income` IS 67000
    `the s 154-20(2) upper threshold` IS 125000
    `I had an accumulated debt on the 1 June` IS TRUE
    `my accumulated debt on that 1 June` IS 3000
    `amounts paid or assessed against that debt` IS 0
    `my Medicare levy is nil or reduced` IS FALSE
    `my other income-contingent loan repayments for the year` IS 0
    `the income year is 2019-20 or later` IS FALSE

-- The least of $1,950, 10% of $80,000 ($8,000) and the $3,000 repayable debt: $1,950, less no other loan repayments.
#ASSERT `How much compulsory repayment must I make` `an accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt` `Jarrah on 80000 with a 3000 debt` EQUALS JUST 1950
#ASSERT `How much compulsory repayment must I make` `an accumulated Student Financial Supplement (FS) debt` `Jarrah on 80000 with a 3000 debt` EQUALS JUST 1950
-- A HELP repayment of $1,950 takes the whole amount: $1,950 - $1,950 = 0, so nothing (s 10F(2)).
#ASSERT `How much compulsory repayment must I make` `an accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt` `Jarrah with HELP repayments of 1950` EQUALS JUST 0
-- $2,000 already paid leaves a $1,000 repayable debt (s 10G), the least of the three; less $500 of HELP repayments: $500.
#ASSERT `How much compulsory repayment must I make` `an accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt` `Jarrah with 1000 left and HELP repayments of 500` EQUALS JUST 500
-- At (not above) the minimum, or with the Medicare levy reduced: nothing.
#ASSERT `How much compulsory repayment must I make` `an accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt` `Jarrah at the minimum` EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much compulsory repayment must I make` `an accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt` `Jarrah with a reduced Medicare levy` EQUALS JUST 0
-- s 12ZLC(1) covers 2019-20 and later; an earlier FS year is not covered.
#ASSERT `How much compulsory repayment must I make` `an accumulated Student Financial Supplement (FS) debt` `an FS debtor in 2018-19` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The same 2018-19 facts for an ABSTUDY SSL debt are not limited by year: $1,950.
#ASSERT `How much compulsory repayment must I make` `an accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt` `an FS debtor in 2018-19` EQUALS JUST 1950

§ `s 43E(5), (6) -- present value`

-- The statute's example (Terry): ($1,200 / 0.1) x [1 - 1 / 1.1^5] = $4,548.94..., which the Act gives as $4,548.
#ASSERT FLOOR (`What is the present value of my unpaid debt` 1200 0.1 5) EQUALS 4548
-- Terry's $4,700 offer is at least the present value; $4,500 would not be.
#ASSERT `Is my offer at least the present value` 4700 1200 0.1 5
#ASSERT NOT `Is my offer at least the present value` 4500 1200 0.1 5
